============= CLI >>browse --help<< =============
usage: ncrystal_browse [options] [PATTERN ...]

Browse and search the data available to NCrystal from built-in sources or
plugins.

Each PATTERN can be:

  - a substring of the data name (e.g. parts of the file name),
  - the name of an element or isotope in the materials (e.g. Al or B10),
  - a condition, such as "absxs>100" or sg==225 (see --cond-help).

Substrings are case-insensitive, but element and isotope names must be written
exactly (e.g. B for boron).

other options:
  -h, --help           show this help message and exit
  --full-help          Show detailed help and exit.
  --cond-help          Show the properties usable in conditions and exit.
  -s, --search WORD    Only show data with WORD in names or comments.
  -x, --extract ENTRY  Print the full content of ENTRY.

examples:
  ncrystal_browse Al_sg225                # data with "al_sg225" in the name
  ncrystal_browse Al                      # name has "al", or material has Al
  ncrystal_browse B10                     # name has "b10", or material has B10
  ncrystal_browse D                       # name has "d", or material has D
  ncrystal_browse "absxs>100"             # strong absorbers
  ncrystal_browse sg==225 "density<3"     # all conditions must be fulfilled
  ncrystal_browse scatknl=yes             # materials with scattering kernels
  ncrystal_browse state!=solid            # liquids, gases, or unknown state
  ncrystal_browse state=liquid H          # liquids with "h" in name, or with H
  ncrystal_browse -s metal                # header comments with "metal"
  ncrystal_browse -x Al_sg225.ncmat       # show the full content

Use --cond-help for the list of properties, and --full-help for all options.

============= CLI >>browse --full-help<< =============
usage: ncrystal_browse [-h] [--full-help] [--cond-help] [-s WORD] [-f SRC]
                       [--json] [--color WHEN] [-x ENTRY]
                       [PATTERN ...]

Browse and search the data available to NCrystal from built-in sources or
plugins.

Each PATTERN can be:

  - a substring of the data name (e.g. parts of the file name),
  - the name of an element or isotope in the materials (e.g. Al or B10),
  - a condition, such as "absxs>100" or sg==225 (see --cond-help).

Substrings are case-insensitive, but element and isotope names must be written
exactly (e.g. B for boron).

Data from all sources is listed, e.g. files in the standard data library,
in-memory data, or data created on-demand like "solid::B4C/2.52gcm3". Files
found relative to the current directory are only listed with "-f relpath".
Element names and conditions require all candidate materials to be loaded.

Listed names include their source (like "stdlib::Al_sg225.ncmat"). When several
sources provide the same name, the first one listed is used when the name is
given without its source.

positional arguments:
  PATTERN               Substring, element, or condition (see above).

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --full-help           Show detailed help and exit.
  --cond-help           Show the properties usable in conditions and exit.

selecting data:
  -s, --search WORD     Only show data which contain WORD in their name or
                        NCMAT header comments (case-insensitive). Can be
                        specified multiple times, in which case all words must
                        be present. Matching comment lines are shown.
  -f, --factory SRC     Only show data from the source SRC (e.g. "stdlib" or
                        "virtual", see "-f help").

output:
  --json                Output all information about the selected data
                        (including physics properties) as JSON.
  --color, --colour WHEN
                        Highlight --search hits: "always", "never", or "auto"
                        (default, only on a terminal).

other:
  -x, --extract ENTRY   Print the full content of ENTRY (e.g. a file name).

examples:
  ncrystal_browse Al_sg225                # data with "al_sg225" in the name
  ncrystal_browse Al                      # name has "al", or material has Al
  ncrystal_browse B10                     # name has "b10", or material has B10
  ncrystal_browse D                       # name has "d", or material has D
  ncrystal_browse "absxs>100"             # strong absorbers
  ncrystal_browse sg==225 "density<3"     # all conditions must be fulfilled
  ncrystal_browse scatknl=yes             # materials with scattering kernels
  ncrystal_browse state!=solid            # liquids, gases, or unknown state
  ncrystal_browse state=liquid H          # liquids with "h" in name, or with H
  ncrystal_browse -s metal                # header comments with "metal"
  ncrystal_browse -x Al_sg225.ncmat       # show the full content

Use --cond-help for the list of properties, and "-f help" for the data sources.

