============= CLI >>browse --cond-help<< =============
conditions:
  Conditions compare a property with a value, like "absxs>100" (conditions with
  < or > need quotes). Text comparisons ignore case. Yes/no values can also be
  given as true/false, on/off, or 1/0.

examples:
  sg=225                        space group 225
  "absxs>100"                   strong absorbers
  state=liquid nelements=2      liquids with two elements
  scatknl=yes                   data with full scattering kernels
  state!=solid                  liquids, gases, or unknown state
  crystal=no                    non-crystalline materials

properties:
  nelements       number of elements
  formula         chemical formula, e.g. Al2O3
  mass            average atomic mass [amu]
  cohsl           average coherent scattering length [fm]
  cohxs           coherent scattering cross section [barn/atom]
  incohxs         incoherent scattering cross section [barn/atom]
  scatxs          free scattering cross section [barn/atom]
  absxs           absorption cross section at 2200m/s [barn/atom]
  density         density [g/cm3]
  numdens         number density [atoms/Aa3]
  state           solid, liquid, gas, or unknown
  crystal         yes or no
  crystalsystem   triclinic, monoclinic, orthorhombic, tetragonal, trigonal,
                  hexagonal, or cubic
  sg              space group number
  natoms          number of atoms in the unit cell
  braggthreshold  Bragg threshold [Aa]
  vdos, vdosdebye, scatknl, freegas, sterile
                  whether some atoms have this type of dynamics (yes or no)
  nphases         number of phases
